.TH DIPIBCG 1 "2026-10-19" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipibcg \- announce or listen for a BiM-encoded TVA guide via DVBSTP/BCG
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipibcg
.B \-a
.B \-s
.I schema
.B \-i
.I input
[\fB\-M\fR \fImap.csv\fR]
.B \-m
.I mcast\fR:\fIport
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B dipibcg
.B \-l
.B \-s
.I schema
.B \-m
.I mcast\fR:\fIport
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipibcg
implements DVB-IPI EPG/BCG (ETSI TS 102 539): it announces TV-Anytime fragments on a multicast
group, BiM-encoded or as plain XML, from an xmltv guide, a TVA XML document or a BiM stream, or
listens on a group and writes the received guide out as xmltv, TVA XML or BiM.
.PP
In announce mode
.RB ( \-a )
it reads the input
.RB ( \-i )
named by
.B \-f
(xmltv, a TVAMain document or a stream of
.BR dipibim (1))
and, for xmltv, an id-to-service mapping
.RB ( \-M ,
an \fIid,uri,tsid,onid,sid\fR csv, same shape as
.BR dipixmltv (1)/\fBdipiscan\fR(1);
id and uri may be double-quoted, with "" for a literal quote)
(of xmltv channels with the same id the first is used, the others are dropped with a warning;
channels missing from the mapping are not announced, also with a warning)
at startup, and again on SIGHUP. Every
.B \-t
(\fB\-\-interval\fR) seconds it re-filters programmes still inside the
announcement window
.RB ( \-w ;
a programme without stop ends at the next start on its channel, the
last one without stop is left out, TS 102 323 8.5),
BiM-encodes what's left, wraps it in a container (Encapsulation structure
with DVB BiM fragment references, TS 102 323 9.3, and data repositories, TS 102 822-3-2
4.5.2.1) and a compression_wrapper (TS 102 323 7.3.1.5), and sends it
via DVBSTP payload 0xA3 (\fBcompr=001\fR, TS 102 539 table 3) on the
given multicast group
.RB ( \-m ).
Each channel is its own container and DVBSTP segment with its own
version, so a changed programme bumps only its channel's segment.
A single channel over 65535 bytes per repository is an error. No TVAMain fragment is sent: it's optional (TS 102 323 9.4.2.2) and
redundant once every fragment carries its own type tag.
.PP
In listen mode
.RB ( \-l )
it joins the multicast group
.RB ( \-m ),
reassembles DVBSTP segments, unwraps the compression_wrapper
(inflating it first if compressed), and after
.B \-t
(\fB\-\-timeout\fR) seconds writes the most recently decoded container
of each segment id, merged, to
.RB ( \-o )
in the format of
.BR \-f .
Segments with compr=001 are BiM, with compr=000 plain TVA XML.
Each cycle is a full snapshot, not incremental: a segment's newer
version replaces the older one. A segment whose wrapper this
build can't decompress (no zlib) is skipped like any other malformed
segment. Optionally
.RB ( \-C )
it also writes back a service mapping csv (real uri/tsid/onid/sid from
the received ServiceInformation fragments), feedable straight back
into a later
.BR \-M .
.PP
.B \-Z
(\fB\-\-compress\fR) zlib-compresses (RFC 1950) the container inside
the wrapper; announce-only, rejected in
.BR \-l .
zlib support depends on the build. Listen mode decompresses transparently and requires no flag.
.PP
Announce encodes against the schema of urn:tva:metadata:2004, or the schema file given with
.BR \-s .
Listen takes the namespace from the DVB-TVA-init (0xA1) and loads that schema through
.BR \-s .
Fragments of types the schema does not code are skipped.
.PP
Schedule fragments carry start/end, chronological events and
PublishedDuration (TS 102 323 8.5). With
.B \-\-publisher
the TVAMain fragment goes out on payload 0xA2, with
.B \-\-index
the TS 102 323 9.5.1 profiled indices on payload 0xA4 (index list in
container 0x0000, sub-indices after the data containers). Listen mode puts
TVAMain publisher and xml:lang into the xmltv output (source-info-name,
lang), decodes the data part of 0xA5 containers and checks received index
containers: structures present, entries ordered, every locator pointing to
a received fragment. Index list entries other than the profiled ones are
ignored (TS 102 323 9.5.1.3).
.PP
SIGHUP re-reads
.B \-i
and
.B \-M
in announce mode. On error, also when the new guide fails to build,
the previous guide keeps being announced and the error is logged.
A guide that fails to build is fatal at startup; later the last built
guide keeps being sent and the build is retried every cycle, its errors
logged once until a build succeeds again.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-announce
Headend mode: read
.BR \-i ,
transmit on
.BR \-m .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen
Client mode: receive on
.BR \-m ,
write
.BR \-o .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " \fIpath\fR"
Announce: xmltv source (required).
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-map " \fIpath\fR"
Announce: xmltv id -> uri,tsid,onid,sid csv (required).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-window " \fIhours\fR"
Announce: only events starting within this window (default 24).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mcast " \fImcast\fR:\fIport\fR"
Multicast group:port (\fB[\fIaddr6\fB]\fR:\fIport\fR for IPv6). Required.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-iface " \fIiface\fR"
Multicast interface. Default: kernel route.
.TP
.BR \-\-dscp " " \fIv\fR
Announce: output DSCP marking (ETSI TS 102 034 Table 29):
.BR video-high ", " video-low ", " voice ", " signalling ", " best-effort ,
or a raw DSCP value 0..63. Default
.BR signalling .
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-ttl " \fIn\fR"
Announce: multicast TTL / IPv6 hop limit, 1..255 (default 16).
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-interval " \fIs\fR"
Announce: repeat interval, minimum 1 (default 5).
.TP
.BR \-\-refresh " \fIn\fR"
Announce: segments whose content changed are sent every cycle, unchanged
ones every Nth cycle, minimum 1 (default 1: all every cycle).
Receivers joining late wait up to N intervals for an unchanged segment.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " \fIs\fR"
Listen: stop after N seconds, 0 runs until SIGINT/SIGTERM (default 35).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIpath\fR"
Listen: xmltv output path, "\-" for stdout (default).
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-csv\-map " \fIpath\fR"
Listen: also write a mapping csv (feeds back into \fB\-M\fR). Off by
default.
.TP
.BR \-Z ", " \-\-compress
Announce: zlib-compress BCG containers (RFC 1950). Off by default;
rejected in listen mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-publisher " \fIdomain\fR/\fIname\fR"
Announce: send the TVAMain fragment (payload 0xA2, TS 102 539 7.4) with this
publisher, TS 102 323 8.9 format, name RFC 3986 encoded. Off by default.
.TP
.BR \-\-lang " \fIlang\fR"
Announce: TVAMain xml:lang (xs:language, e.g. de\-AT). Requires
.BR \-\-publisher .
.TP
.BR \-\-index " \fIkind\fR[,\fIkind\fR...]"
Announce: send TS 102 323 9.5.1 profiled index containers (payload 0xA4,
index list in container 0x0000). Kinds:
.BR pi\-crid ,
.BR pi\-title ,
.BR schedule\-time ,
.BR schedule\-title .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fIfmt\fR"
.IR xmltv | tva | bim .
Announce: format of the input at \fB\-i\fR. tva is a TVAMain document, bim a stream written by
.BR "dipibim \-\-profile dvb\-tva" .
tva and bim input must meet the TS 102 323 clause 8 content rules, a violation fails the load.
Listen: format of the output: xmltv, one TVA XML document or such a bim stream. Default: \fBxmltv\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-encoding " \fIenc\fR"
.IR bim | plain .
Announce: BiM (compr=001, default) or plain TVA XML with compr=000 on the same payload ids.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-schema " \fIpath\fR"
TV-Anytime schema file, or directory searched recursively for the schema of the namespace
(announce: urn:tva:metadata:2004, listen: SchemaURI[0] of the stream). Repeatable. One schema
file is used as is and its namespace is sent as SchemaURI[0], of several files the one declaring the namespace is used.
Further schemas of a stream's DecoderInit are found the same way, the chunks of those not found are skipped.
Announce lists the namespaces of a \fB\-f tva\fR document that the main schema does not define as further schemas,
when a schema file for them is found. Required.
.TP
.B \-\-dvb\-locator
Announce: optimized locator coding where the decoder renders the same text.
.TP
.B \-\-dvb\-duration
Announce: minute coding of durations where exact.
.TP
.B \-\-dvb\-pubtime
Announce: PublishedTime coding of dateTime where representable.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Periodic stats on stderr: one line per cycle in announce mode, one
line per segment in listen mode.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fIwhen\fR
auto|always|never (default auto).
.TP
.B \-\-metrics \fIpath\fR
Announce only. Unix datagram socket for metrics (default:
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock ).
Rejected without \fB\-\-metrics\-id\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-id \fIname\fR
Announce only. Stable instance id; metrics disabled unless set.
Rejected in listen mode.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-interval \fIs\fR
Announce only. Snapshot interval in seconds (default 5). Rejected
without \fB\-\-metrics\-id\fR.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config\ \fI<path>\fR
YAML configuration file. Keys mirror the options above. Without this option,
.I /etc/dvbipitools/dipibcg.yaml
is read if it exists.
.TP
.B \-\-config\-strict
Treat configuration file issues (unknown or duplicate keys, invalid values,
conflicting settings, unreadable referenced files) as errors instead of
warnings.
.TP
.B \-\-configtest
Check the configuration file (from
.B \-c
or the default location) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipibcg \-a \-i guide.xml \-M mapping.csv \-m 239.255.0.2:3938
Announce guide.xml on the given multicast group using mapping.csv.
.TP
.B dipibcg \-l \-m 239.255.0.2:3938 \-o guide.xml \-C mapping.csv
Listen on the group, write the received guide to guide.xml and a
service mapping to mapping.csv.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dvbipitools/dipibcg.yaml
Default configuration file, read if present. A commented template with all
defaults ships as
.IR /usr/share/dvbipitools/etc/dipibcg.yaml .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipixmltv (1),
.BR dipibim (1),
.BR dipiscan (1),
.BR dipisds (1)
.PP
